humanize is used to format datetime objects into human-readable relative time strings, like "a moment ago", "2 hours ago", or "in 3 days".
It's called via:
arrow.Arrow.humanize()
Examples:
import arrow

now = arrow.now()
past = now.shift(hours=-2)
future = now.shift(days=3)

past.humanize()       # "2 hours ago"
future.humanize()     # "in 3 days"
now.humanize()        # "just now"





