there is an issue with humanize() in arrow.py: calibration for the month is inaccurate. what is the issue exactly? give an example

The issue is at arrow.py:1211-1216. The cutoff self._SECS_PER_MONTH = 30.5 days is too short.
Concrete example:
arw = arrow.Arrow(2024, 1, 15)       # Jan 15
later = arw.shift(months=1)           # Feb 15 = 31 days later
arw.humanize(later)                   # ❌ "a month ago" (correct)

arw = arrow.Arrow(2024, 1, 31)        # Jan 31
later = arw.shift(months=1)           # Feb 29 = 29 days later
arw.humanize(later)                   # ❌ "4 weeks ago" instead of "a month ago"
Why: 29 days = 2,505,600 seconds, but _SECS_PER_MONTH = 2,638,800 (30.5 days). Since 29 < 30.5, it falls into the "weeks" branch instead of "month". A calendar month shift of ~29-31 days can be reported as "4 weeks" when it should say "a month".

